      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mscpyy9tq2851h4o",
          "message": {
            "text": "Verified against real engines, not just the mocks: a genuine PG17 cluster is built, then the application's own getDb() upgrades it.\n\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  3 passed (3)\n  Duration  7.28s\n\nThe fixture deliberately drops reviewfiles.differencescore before migrating, reproducing the realistic case where a user is several schema versions behind rather than a same-schema copy. The test asserts the column is present again afterward, since the staged target is built by the app's own initSchema — the major upgrade and the ordinary column migrations happen in one pass.\n\nAlso confirmed against a copy of the maintainer's real 35 MB database: 1481 rows across 6 tables, validateMigration('full').ok = true, and three adversarial mutations (a changed cell, a deleted row, a dropped source column) each still fail validation — so the check is not vacuous.\n\nThe unit tests were separately confirmed non-vacuous by breaking the source: making blocked fall through to quarantine fails the connection test, and swapping despite failed validation fails the migrate-major test.\n",
            "markdown": "Verified against real engines, not just the mocks: a genuine PG17 cluster is built, then the application's own `getDb()` upgrades it.\n\n```\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  3 passed (3)\n  Duration  7.28s\n```\n\nThe fixture deliberately drops `review_files.difference_score` before migrating, reproducing the realistic case where a user is several schema versions behind rather than a same-schema copy. The test asserts the column is present again afterward, since the staged target is built by the app's own `initSchema` — the major upgrade and the ordinary column migrations happen in one pass.\n\nAlso confirmed against a copy of the maintainer's real 35 MB database: 1481 rows across 6 tables, `validateMigration('full').ok = true`, and three adversarial mutations (a changed cell, a deleted row, a dropped source column) each still fail validation — so the check is not vacuous.\n\nThe unit tests were separately confirmed non-vacuous by breaking the source: making `blocked` fall through to quarantine fails the connection test, and swapping despite failed validation fails the migrate-major test.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "tests/integration/db/major-migration.test.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 25,
                  "endLine": 33,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "\ndescribe.skipIf(!live)('major-version migration (live PG17 -> PG18)', () => {\n  let root: string;\n  let dbPath: string;\n\n  beforeAll(async () => {\n    root = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'glassbox-migrate-'));\n    dbPath = join(root, 'data', 'reviews');\n    mkdirSync(join(root, 'data'), { recursive: true });"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "test-evidence"
            ]
          },
          "workItemUris": [
            "GB-875"
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
